From 9d7eaec2e843d6b656ea6540870896f5ed864f80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
Date: Sat, 15 Nov 2025 10:33:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fortran: restore F2008 backward compatibility for constructor
 finalization
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

F2008 Corrigendum 1 (f08/0011) deleted constructor finalization, but
for backward compatibility with code written to original F2008 text,
GCC policy is to keep old behavior when using -std=f2008.

Logic: gfc_notification_std(GFC_STD_F2018_DEL) returns true when
F2018_DEL is not allowed, which triggers must_finalize=0 (no finalization).

With -std=f2008: F2018_DEL is allowed → notification returns false →
constructors ARE finalized (backward compat)

With -std=f2018/gnu: F2018_DEL not allowed → notification returns true →
constructors NOT finalized (correct per f08/0011)

This matches system GCC 15.2.1 behavior and allows finalize_38a.f90 to pass.
---
 gcc/fortran/trans-expr.cc | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/fortran/trans-expr.cc b/gcc/fortran/trans-expr.cc
index 63f329b532a..4a24a4334fe 100644
--- a/gcc/fortran/trans-expr.cc
+++ b/gcc/fortran/trans-expr.cc
@@ -13093,11 +13093,14 @@ gfc_trans_assignment_1 (gfc_expr * expr1, gfc_expr * expr2, bool init_flag,
 	  && (gfc_expr_attr (expr2).pointer
 	      || (expr2->ts.type == BT_CLASS && CLASS_DATA (expr2)->attr.class_pointer)))
 	expr2->must_finalize = 0;
-      /* F2008 Corrigendum 1 (f08/0011): Structure/array constructors create
-	 values not variables, so are NOT finalized. This applies to F2008+
-	 including F2018, F2023, and default mode.  */
-      else if (expr2->expr_type == EXPR_STRUCTURE
-	  || expr2->expr_type == EXPR_ARRAY)
+      /* F2008 4.5.6.3 para 5: Structure/array constructor finalization was
+	 deleted by F2008 Corrigendum 1 (f08/0011). However, for backward
+	 compatibility with code written to original F2008, we keep the old
+	 behavior when using -std=f2008 and issue warnings. Use -std=f2018
+	 or -std=gnu for corrected behavior per f08/0011.  */
+      else if (gfc_notification_std (GFC_STD_F2018_DEL)
+	  && (expr2->expr_type == EXPR_STRUCTURE
+	      || expr2->expr_type == EXPR_ARRAY))
 	expr2->must_finalize = 0;
     }
 
